    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/2/82646.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 126,
    "turn_text": "Good luck to the campaign going forward. All right, we have a rare glimpse of the president's press secretary today. She gave a lot of excuses for why White House briefings have gone the way of the dodo extinct. Are they ever coming back to life? The interesting part is the explanation, and it has spawned an argument for you next. Stephanie Grisham. Can you place the face? She's the White House press secretary, almost three months now. Many of you may not know that. She's never stood behind the podium in the White House press briefing room to take questions from reporters. A press secretary who does not take questions from the press. And today, over on State TV, she gave several excuses for the moratorium. Number one, the briefings are useless, she says, because the press can just ask the president.",
